# DOC Manager — architecture & delivery

Stack: Next.js 15 App Router · React 19 · Tailwind 4 · Supabase · Tesseract · DeepSeek · TanStack Query · Turborepo · Render.

## Monorepo layout

```
apps/web            # UI + Route Handlers (BFF)
apps/worker-ocr     # OCR / classify / PDF jobs
apps/worker-notify  # email + WhatsApp (Twilio)
packages/ui         # @ac/ui design system
packages/shared     # @ac/shared enums, Zod, event contracts
packages/db         # migrations / generated types (or supabase/)
supabase/migrations
```

## Non-negotiable decisions

- **Queue in Postgres** (`document_jobs` / pg-boss) — no Kafka/RabbitMQ.
- **Search in Postgres** (tsvector + GIN + `pg_trgm`) — no Elasticsearch.
- **Archive is metadata-driven** — do not move Storage objects to “organize”.
- **OCR and heavy PDF work only in workers** — never in the browser / Route Handler sync path.
- **DeepSeek responses must pass Zod** before persist; low confidence → `needs_review`.
- **Multi-tenant via `org_id` + RLS**; no service-role usage in client code.
- **Single contract source:** `@ac/shared` shared by web + workers.

## Delivery order (do not skip ahead)

**Backend (Jira `E0`–`E15`):** scaffolding/contracts → DB/Auth/RLS → upload skeleton → jobs → OCR (+ calibration) → DeepSeek → taxonomy → search → workflow/ERP → share → PDF → notify → Giulia → PWA → RGPD → release.

**UI (Jira `UI0`–`UI14`):** Design System → layouts → navigation → pages as composition → motion → polish.

Never build Landing/Dashboard/feature pages before `@ac/ui` tokens + primitives exist. Prefer composing existing components over new one-offs.

## UI / design system

- Tokens and components live in `packages/ui`; apps consume, don’t fork styles.
- Design language: premium AI SaaS (Vercel/Linear/Stripe-like) — white surfaces, **blue accents**, large spacing, high radius, soft shadows, enterprise minimalism. Brand **DOC Manager**.
- Prefer design tokens / theme classes over one-off hex and arbitrary Tailwind values.
- Icons: Lucide via shared `Icon` wrapper (size/stroke/color standardized).
- Full UI workflow/quality bar: see `ai-development-workflow` rule.

## Jira conventions

- Technical: `[E{n}.{mm}] …` under workstreams `DM` labels `etapa-n`.
- UI: `[UI{n}.{mm}] …` labels `ui`, `ui-etapa-n`.
- OCR filter calibration: `[E4.06]` / harness in `worker-ocr` only.
- When implementing a ticket: respect **Paths**, **Depende de**, **Fora de escopo** on the issue.
- AI status path only: **In Progress** → **Testing** → **Completed AI** (never **Completed Human**).

## Parallel tracks

UI can advance on mocks while backend tickets land, but **API/UI contracts must match `@ac/shared`**. Do not invent a second DTO shape in the frontend.
